messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "AI systems do most routine computer-based knowledge tasks at or above typical human level.",
      "detail": "Adoption lags capability, but software, research assistance and office work begin to be reorganised around AI agents."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Humans return to the surface of the Moon.",
      "detail": "The United States, China or both land crews, starting a slow build-up toward permanent lunar outposts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2031,
      "event": "Global average warming passes 1.5°C above pre-industrial on a sustained basis.",
      "detail": "Heat waves, fires, floods and crop shocks become more frequent, while emissions plateau and begin a slow decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "AI that matches or exceeds human experts across nearly all cognitive tasks is widely acknowledged.",
      "detail": "The date is uncertain by a decade or more either way. AI begins to substantially accelerate its own development and scientific research."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "A major AI-enabled crisis forces binding international AI governance.",
      "detail": "The trigger is most likely a large cyber, biological or loss-of-control incident. This period carries the highest risk of permanent catastrophe; I put the chance of existential disaster this century at roughly 10–20%."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Automation displaces a large share of human labour, and states introduce large-scale redistribution.",
      "detail": "Wages stop being the main source of income for many people. Political turmoil is severe in some countries and outcomes are unequal."
    },
    {
      "year": 2046,
      "event": "The first humans land on Mars.",
      "detail": "The mission is enabled by cheap heavy launch and robotic pre-deployment. It is symbolically large but economically marginal."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "AI-driven biomedicine makes most cancers and many infectious and genetic diseases curable or manageable.",
      "detail": "Life expectancy rises quickly where access exists. Engineered-pandemic risk also rises and requires constant biosurveillance."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "A nuclear weapon is used in conflict for the first time since 1945.",
      "detail": "I consider at least one limited use more likely than not within the next century, though the timing is a guess. It most likely remains regional rather than civilisation-ending."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "Global warming passes 2°C.",
      "detail": "Coral reefs are largely lost, and parts of the tropics see dangerous heat extremes and significant migration."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "World population peaks at roughly 9.5 billion and begins to decline.",
      "detail": "Fertility is below replacement almost everywhere. Ageing societies depend on machine labour."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global net-zero carbon emissions are reached.",
      "detail": "Very cheap solar, storage, fission and early fusion make it possible. Warming peaks later at about 2.3–2.7°C."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "Machines perform the vast majority of economic, scientific and military work.",
      "detail": "Humans act mainly as owners, voters and setters of goals. How much real control they retain is the key unresolved question."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Ageing is substantially slowed, and healthy lifespans beyond 120 become attainable.",
      "detail": "Sea level is about 0.6 m higher than in 2000. The world is far richer on average but politically unrecognisable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Digital minds, including emulated or uploaded human minds, are legally recognised as persons in major jurisdictions.",
      "detail": "Digital persons soon outnumber biological ones, since they can be copied and run fast."
    },
    {
      "year": 2160,
      "event": "Space industry, mostly robotic, becomes a major part of the economy.",
      "detail": "Thousands of biological humans live permanently off Earth. Machines mining and manufacturing on the Moon and asteroids vastly outnumber them."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Atmospheric CO2 is being actively drawn down and Earth's climate is deliberately managed.",
      "detail": "Temperatures are steered back toward pre-industrial levels over centuries. Ice-sheet loss continues to raise seas regardless."
    },
    {
      "year": 2260,
      "event": "The first interstellar probes are launched at a meaningful fraction of light speed.",
      "detail": "Small, intelligent, self-repairing craft head to nearby stars, powered by beamed energy or fusion."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Sea level stands 2–4 m above the 2000 level, and the biological human population has fallen below 4 billion.",
      "detail": "Coastal cities have been moved, defended or abandoned. Population decline is voluntary and cushioned by abundance."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Off-Earth settlements become fully self-sufficient.",
      "detail": "Habitats on Mars, on the Moon and in free space could survive the loss of Earth. This sharply lowers extinction risk from any single catastrophe."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Unmodified biological humans are a small minority of all persons.",
      "detail": "Most minds are digital, heavily augmented or hybrid. Baseline humans persist by choice and are protected by law or custom."
    },
    {
      "year": 2650,
      "event": "A VEI-7 super-colossal volcanic eruption occurs somewhere on Earth.",
      "detail": "Such eruptions occur roughly once or twice per millennium, so the date is purely illustrative. A technological civilisation absorbs the cooling with little loss."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Probes arrive in nearby star systems and begin building infrastructure from local materials.",
      "detail": "Alpha Centauri and other systems within about 15 light-years gain self-replicating industrial footholds."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Civilisation's energy use exceeds the total sunlight falling on Earth.",
      "detail": "Solar collectors and habitats across the inner solar system hold most activity. Earth is increasingly treated as a heritage and nature preserve."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Permanent societies of digital and engineered beings exist around several nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Light-speed delays make them politically and culturally independent of the solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Humanity's descendants have diverged into many distinct biological and non-biological lineages.",
      "detail": "The word \"human\" becomes a term of ancestry rather than a description of a single species."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "No language spoken today survives as a natural living tongue.",
      "detail": "Today's languages and cultures are preserved in complete archives and revived by enthusiasts. Everyday communication is unrecognisable."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "A partial Dyson swarm captures a noticeable fraction of the Sun's output.",
      "detail": "Most of it powers computation. Earth's biosphere is largely restored, with engineered de-extinctions."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "The settled region reaches roughly 100 light-years from the Sun.",
      "detail": "Expansion proceeds at a few percent of light speed. No sign of extraterrestrial intelligence has been found, which is my best guess but far from certain."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Star systems drift apart in values, and some conflict occurs between them.",
      "detail": "No unified government is possible across interstellar distances. Loose shared protocols and a common origin are the main ties."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Earth's climate is held stable, averting the natural drift toward the next glaciation.",
      "detail": "Earth holds perhaps a few hundred million biological humans. They live in a deliberately maintained Holocene-like world."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Thousands of star systems are inhabited.",
      "detail": "The vast majority of minds descended from humanity have never been to the solar system. Old Earth history is studied as deep antiquity."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilisation spans several hundred light-years, and recognisable biological humans still exist as a small minority.",
      "detail": "This is the central case if the 21st and 22nd centuries are survived. The specific dates after about 2100 are illustrative only."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "I expect the next century or two to be the decisive and most dangerous period, dominated by the arrival of superhuman AI, with perhaps a 10–25% chance of extinction or permanent loss of human control. If that passage is survived, I expect human-descended minds, mostly digital or heavily modified, to spread through the solar system and to nearby stars, with baseline biological humans surviving as a protected minority. So my best guess is that humanity exists in the year 10000, though greatly transformed, and every date after about 2100 is highly uncertain."
}
